    three screens above it. The breadth reveal's own zoom link points at the same #calc,
    so the glance and the detail share one target. */}
<section id="true-cost">
  <CountryDoor country={c} />

  <GutPunch country={c} />

  <BreadthReveal country={c} />

  <div id="calc" class="tc-number">
  <p class="lab">The number</p>
  <h2>What you'll really spend in {c.name}.</h2>
  <p class="sub">Your flights if you want them counted, your room, your on-the-ground spending, the two fees most US cards add without telling you, and {c.name}'s tourist tax. One number, nothing waiting on the statement. No bank to pick, no sign-up, nothing saved.</p>
  {/* A thin strip rather than the full 16:9. The full crop ran close to a whole phone screen
      and pushed the controls a screen below the section's own promise, which is a lot of
      decoration to scroll past on the way to a calculator. Cropped in CSS from the existing
      asset, so no new image is needed and the file is untouched.
      The secart-thin modifier is deliberate: .secart is shared with the currency and traps
      sections, and thinning those was not asked for. Only this instance changes. */}
  {art && <figure class="secart secart-thin"><img src={art.cost} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1400" height="788" /></figure>}

  <!-- Everything the module needs, handed over as inert JSON (Astro leaves application/json untouched). No card data ships: it asks the traveler nothing about their own card. -->
  <script type="application/json" id="hn-data" set:html={calcJson}></script>

  <div class="estimator" id="hn-app" hidden>
    <div class="erow">
      <div class="ef ef-room">
        <label for="hnRoom">Hotel price a night</label>
        <span class="moneyin"><span class="mny">$</span><input id="hnRoom" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="150" aria-label="Hotel price per night in US dollars" /></span>
      </div>
      <label class="hn-toggle hn-toggle-inline" id="hnPaidWrap">
        <input type="checkbox" id="hnPaid" />
        <span class="hn-switch" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hn-toggle-l">Already paid for the room</span>
      </label>
    </div>
    <p class="ef-hint-room" id="hnRoomHint" hidden></p>

    <label class="cf hn-region" id="hnRegionWrap" hidden style="display:none">
      <span class="cf-l">Where are you staying?</span>
      <span class="selwrap"><select id="hnRegion"></select></span>
    </label>

    <div class="erow erow-flight">
      <div class="ef ef-flight">
        <label for="hnFlight">Flights, round trip a person</label>
        <span class="moneyin"><span class="mny">$</span><input id="hnFlight" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="" aria-label="Round trip flight price per traveler in US dollars" /></span>
      </div>
      <p class="ef-hint" id="hnFlightHint">Optional. Enter your round trip fare per traveler to fold flights into the total.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="erow">
      <div class="ef ef-num"><label>Travelers</label>
        <span class="stepper">
          <button type="button" class="stp" data-step="hnTrav" data-dir="-1" aria-label="One fewer traveler">&#8722;</button>
          <span class="stp-v" id="hnTrav" data-v="2">2</span>
          <button type="button" class="stp" data-step="hnTrav" data-dir="1" aria-label="One more traveler">+</button>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="ef ef-num"><label>Nights</label>
        <span class="stepper">
          <button type="button" class="stp" data-step="hnNights" data-dir="-1" aria-label="One fewer night">&#8722;</button>
          <span class="stp-v" id="hnNights" data-v="7">7</span>
          <button type="button" class="stp" data-step="hnNights" data-dir="1" aria-label="One more night">+</button>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="ef ef-style"><label>Style</label>
        <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Travel style">
          {c.cash.styles.map((s, i) => (
            <button id={"hnStyle" + i} class={i === c.cash.defaultIndex ? "on" : ""} type="button" data-per={s.per} data-cash={s.cash} data-room={s.room}>{s.n}</button>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <CalcResult country={c} tipCalc={tipCalc} />
  </div>

  <noscript>
    <div class="reveal"><div class="t">The full total needs JavaScript switched on. With it off: take your round trip flights and the room price, add your on-the-ground spending, add about 3% for a typical US card's foreign fee on what you put on the card, a few dollars plus about 3% for each ATM cash withdrawal, and {c.name}'s tourist tax.</div></div>
  </noscript>

  {/* THE TTC-ED CARD. Foot of the calculator, so it summarizes the numbers directly above
      it. It mirrors the calculator's own rendered figures rather than recomputing them, so
      it cannot disagree with the block it summarizes, and it hides itself if the calculator
      did not run. The affiliate card shortlist below is an appendix to the calculator
      rather than part of it, which is why the payoff card sits above it. */}
  <TTCedCard country={c} />

  <details class="cardlist" id="calcNoFee" open>
    <summary class="cardlist-sum">
      <svg class="acc-ico" width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0A5644" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="margin-top:2px" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="5" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M2 10h20"/></svg>
      <span class="cardlist-txt"><b>Not sure which card to bring?</b> See <span class="cardlist-link">my pick for {c.name}</span>.</span>
      <svg class="cardlist-chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="cardlist-body">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:9px;align-items:flex-start;background:#E1F1EB;border-radius:12px;padding:11px 13px;margin:0 0 14px">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#15803D" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex:none;margin-top:1px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:#0A5644"><b>Already carry a card with no foreign transaction fee?</b> Then you are set for {c.name}, and can skip this. There is nothing to buy.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="sl-intro">{shortlist[0] && shortlist[0].kind === "debit"
        ? `${c.name} leans on cash more than its reputation suggests, so the card that earns its place is a fee-free ATM debit card, with a no-foreign-fee credit card for hotels and bigger spots. If you are getting one, this is the pairing I would pick.`
        : `If you are getting a card for ${c.name}, this is the pairing I would pick: a no-foreign-fee credit card for spending, and a fee-free ATM debit card for cash.`} We earn nothing on these today. Always confirm the current fee with the issuer before you apply. Checked {cardsChecked}.</p>
      <div class="sl-row" role="list">
        {shortlist.map((card, i) => (
          <div class="sl" role="listitem">
            {i === 0 && <div style="margin:0"><span style="display:inline-block;background:#0A5644;color:#fff;font-size:11px;font-weight:500;padding:2px 10px;border-radius:999px">My pick for {c.name}</span></div>}
            <div class="sl-face" style={`--f:${faceColors[i % faceColors.length]}`}>
              <div class="sl-top"><span class="sl-bank">{card.issuer}</span><span class="sl-chip" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
              <div class="sl-stripe" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <span class="sl-prod">{card.product}</span>
              <div class="sl-foot"><span class="sl-net">{(card.network || '').toUpperCase()}</span><span class="sl-mark" aria-hidden="true">TTC</span></div>
            </div>
            <p class="sl-why">{(i === 0 && card.note) ? card.note : whyLine(card)}</p>
            <div style="margin:0"><span style="display:inline-block;background:#E1F1EB;color:#0A5644;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:500;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:999px">{card.kind === "debit" ? "Best for ATM cash" : "Best for hotels, shops, dining"}</span></div>
            <span class={"tg " + (card.affiliate && card.affiliate.link ? "earn" : "free")}>{(card.affiliate && card.affiliate.label) || "we earn nothing"}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      {/* Wise multi-currency card: its own quick-card, distinct from the three merit
          picks above. A different job (holding and spending in the local currency, not
          the ATM-cash or credit-card slots) and the one option here with a live program,
          so it carries its own honest label and the only click-through in the panel. The
          button and label are data-driven from cards.js exactly like every other paid
          pick: the button appears only once the tracking link is set, and never before. */}
      <div class="sl-wise">
        <img class="sl-wise-logo" src="/wise-logo.png" alt="Wise" width="262" height="69" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="sl-wise-body">
          <p class="sl-wise-lead"><b>Want one account that holds and spends in the local currency?</b> A different job from the three above, and the one I reach for abroad. It is free to open; you can create a virtual card in the app and add it to your phone wallet in minutes, without waiting for the physical card; and you can convert US dollars into the local currency inside the account before you travel, then spend from that balance. {wiseNote}</p>
          <div class="sl-wise-foot">
            {ext(wiseLink).target && (
              <a class="pickbtn" href={wiseLink} {...ext(wiseLink)}>See the Wise card<span class="arw">&#8594;</span><NewTab /></a>
            )}
            <span class={commLabel(wiseLink).cls}>{commLabel(wiseLink).text}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="display:flex;gap:9px;align-items:flex-start;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:11px 13px;margin:14px 0 0">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0A5644" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex:none;margin-top:1px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 7.5-7 9-4-1.5-7-4.5-7-9V6z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#5C6661">The three picks above pay us nothing, and their tags say so. Wise is the only option here that can earn us a commission, and its tag says that too. Paid or not, the pick is still the pick.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>
  </div>

  {/* THE ARRIVAL CLOSER, the parting site-level thesis. It sits here, immediately after
      the calculator (and after the TTC-ed card once phase 4 lands), because that is the
      flow the brief specifies: door, gut-punch, breadth reveal, calculator, card, closer.
      Note that the guide body continues below it with seasonality, culture and the
      related-countries list, so this is the end of the TRUE-COST FLOW rather than the last
      thing on the page. If it should instead be the final word before the signup prompt,
